# ── Batch FIDE‑name normalisation cache service ──────────────────────────────
#
# Secret API key for the player-name normalisation cache. NEVER commit a real
# value — this file documents the variable name only.
#
# Two uses, same variable:
#
#   1. BUILDING official chess-db releases — the key is baked into the binary via
#      option_env! so the shipped client can call the cache service:
#          CHESSVAULT_NORMALISE_API_KEY=<secret> cargo build -p chess-db --release
#      Build WITHOUT it (normal development) and the cache is simply disabled:
#      `players normalise` runs FIDE-only. Nothing in the public repo to misuse.
#
#   2. RUNNING the service (lpdo-normalise-service) — it requires the same key on
#      every request (Authorization: Bearer <key>) and refuses to start unset.
#
# The service URL is a public compiled-in constant (https://normalise.lpdo.com/normalise);
# only the key is secret. Override per-run with `--service-url` / `--service-key`.
CHESSVAULT_NORMALISE_API_KEY=
